{"id": "EUVD-2026-101127", "enisaUuid": "b006a739-5ab1-3e3b-980d-fd86a2432b8a", "description": "libzvbi through 0.2.45 contains an out-of-bounds write vulnerability in the Teletext decoder that allows attackers to corrupt memory by supplying unvalidated DRCS pixel-mode values in X/28/3 packets. Attackers can send a crafted Teletext stream decoded via vbi_decode with every slot set to DRCS_MODE_6_5_4, causing convert_drcs to overflow chars[48][60] and crash the application.", "datePublished": "2026-10-14T15:01:21", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-20T01:26:18", "baseScore": 6.9, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:N/VI:L/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@haind-pwn/zvbi-teletext-drcs-mode-oob-write", "https://github.com/zapping-vbi/zvbi/blob/d3a5ee9f2b047bf16cd1ee5ccf6ec05ee75409d0/src/packet.c#L447", "https://github.com/zapping-vbi/zvbi", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/libzvbi-through-0.2.45-out-of-bounds-write-via-teletext-drcs-convert-drcs"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-110654", "GHSA-pw98-3fpx-6f7v"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "55b11d23-71fd-3d3b-acbe-9aa3fccc9e90", "product": {"name": "libzvbi", "vendor": {"name": "n/a"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22640.2.45"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "d643528d-35d7-3454-9aea-34d482d687c2", "vendor": {"name": "zapping-vbi"}}], "isExploited": false}